WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:05.029
Hey YouTubers it's Charlie! Thank you everybody
that submitted questions on my Game of Thrones

00:00:05.029 --> 00:00:09.550
video yesterday. Everyone completely upset
about what happened in the episode actually

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:12.700
just careful for spoilers if you haven't seen the episode
so we can start talking about it.

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:17.340
In case you guys didn't see Dan and Dave said
that George RR Martin explained to them what

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:21.160
was going to happen to Shireen eventually.
So that's why she ended up getting put to

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:25.029
the torch so even though it hasn't happened
in the books yet he implied that it would

00:00:25.029 --> 00:00:29.520
be happening or it would have happened had
events gone down that way. Just to clarify, George

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:33.780
RR Martin said that because of the changes
the show has made, people will be dying on

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:38.030
the show that did not die in the books so
what he's done with Dan and Dave is help them

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:43.059
with the character arcs. So given the circumstances
that Stannis is faced with, this is the decision

00:00:43.059 --> 00:00:46.309
that George RR Martin felt he would've made--
the gamble he would've made. It's a really

00:00:46.309 --> 00:00:50.920
big gamble. He is betting that Melisandre is
right. Even though Shireen isn't dead in the

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:54.969
books right now she probably would've ended
up that way. It just might end up happening up at

00:00:54.969 --> 00:01:00.250
the wall. That's what the implication is. Okay, so on to questions. Brian Gieson: do you think what happened to

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:04.729
Shireen in the show will happen in the books as well? Based on what George RR Martin said,

00:01:04.729 --> 00:01:08.969
Yes, it will happen. Probably in a slightly different way though and for slightly different reasons.

00:01:08.969 --> 00:01:13.340
In the books, Stannis left Shireen at
the wall whenever he marched onto Winterfell.

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:17.130
So if she's going to be sacrificed, it's not going to be until stannis gets back. And there are a lot

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:22.200
of spoiler theories as to why Melisandre might
need more king's blood up at the wall. We can

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:26.759
talk about that after the finale though so just put a bookmark in that. Next question, Black Fire

00:01:26.759 --> 00:01:31.609
asks: So now that Stannis has burned his daughter and drank the last of Mel's lord of light

00:01:31.609 --> 00:01:36.069
